{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen identity test modules contain 20 audited leading docstrings (1,567 before-words), frozen at `origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84`. Revalidation incorporates the merged retirement of the `verify-authorship` alias: current positive-path prose names `verify-identity`, while the old name survives only in the negative-control command that must remain executable and unchanged.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the frozen prose blocks below. A `D:<owner>` is the leading `Expr(Constant(str))` in a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`. A `C:<scope>:before:<anchor>` is one maximal consecutive full-line COMMENT-token region, owned by the innermost AST scope and anchored to the next unchanged non-comment code. Compact `D{a,b}` and `C{scope@anchor,...}` notation expands to those exact IDs under the row's path; the reviewer writes the fully path-qualified `<path>#<ID>`.\n\nFor every owned path, retain immutable before and final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies remove only allowlisted leading docstring nodes; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining `ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False)` values to match. Tokenize both blobs and reject changed inline comments or non-allowlisted full-line comments. Preserve runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Only adjacent blank-line normalization around an edited block is allowed.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_3183_heldout.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_3183.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_4e9d_heldout.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_4e9d.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ac1_401a_heldout.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ac1_401a.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ac7_bff8_heldout.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ac7_bff8.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_bde5_heldout.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_bde5.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ddbe_heldout.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ddbe.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_enforce_since_grandfather.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_gate_archived_and_unresolvable_heldout.py` — `D{<module>,test_unresolvable_null_commit_ledger_does_not_fail_gate}`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_perf_1cc0.py` — `D{<module>,test_gate_does_not_call_per_event_resolver}`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ts1_c96d_heldout.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_ts1_c96d.py` — `D:<module>`\n\n## Protected false positives\nEvery full-line comment and every unlisted function/helper docstring is protected; these short blocks state local assertions or fixture constraints without removable history. Preserve all SSH/noqa/type-ignore directives and every CLI argv literal, especially the rejected `verify-authorship` and accepted `verify-identity` commands.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\nKeep replay-never-rejects, signed/unsigned ledgers, write-gate and snapshot behavior; all four event composers and attribution cache; private-key rejection; verify-identity alias removal, since/JSON/CI contracts; identity-scoped trust roots; entity exemptions/resolver fallback; archived/unknown/ledger-era handling; one-pass commit resolution; and in-toto DSSE semantics. `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py` is the real path consumer of the AC7 held-out module. No allowlisted docstring is imported or read through `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only the declared stable-ID blocks and adjacent blank lines change; the AST and token/comment comparisons pass on every owned path.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and retains the listed current contract while removing chronology, duplication, obvious narration, or separator ornament.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts exactly 20 leaf-linked TSV rows: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [ ] Before citations use `d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84:<path>#<stable-id>`; final citations use `<final-commit-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>`; every row has `after_words < before_words` and records `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] All five structured verify commands pass.\n\n## Verification\nThe five DD-level commands recorded on this ticket run focused pytest with real consumers, scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify`. They are the executable completion oracle."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788626357945657550,"uuid":"b3bedc2f-afbb-41ad-bdcc-5bfc12359407"}